            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I assume you mean this failed test:\r\n```\r\nFAIL in tests/test_move.lua | move_line() | has no side effects:\r\n  Failed expectation for equality.\r\n  Left:  {\r\n    points_to = \"1\",\r\n    regcontents = { \"aaa\" },\r\n    regtype = \"V\"\r\n  }\r\n  Right: {\r\n    points_to = \"1\",\r\n    regcontents = { \"wor\" },\r\n    regtype = \"V\"\r\n  }\r\n  Traceback:\r\n    tests/test_move.lua:1139\r\n```\r\nThis is actually catching a different bug not caused by setting only `points_to`.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/cf81e70e8f1fdc36a3c684efc45c4ee561285137/lua/mini/move.lua#L352 Here, `\"zdd` actually sets multiple registers:\r\n- `z` is set to the text of the deleted line as intended\r\n- The numbered registers are shifted up and `1` is also set to the line's text, as if `dd` was executed with no specified register\r\n- `\"` is pointed to the `1` register\r\n\r\nI believe this is actually a bug in Nvim, as `:help quote1` clearly states:\r\n> Numbered register 1 contains the text deleted by the most recent delete or change command, **unless the command specified another register** or the text is less than one line (the small delete register is used then).\r\n\r\nThis also happens with `\"zx`: https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/cf81e70e8f1fdc36a3c684efc45c4ee561285137/lua/mini/move.lua#L232\r\n\r\nA workaround is to yank into `z`, then delete into the black hole register:\r\n```patch\r\n--- a/lua/mini/move.lua\r\n+++ b/lua/mini/move.lua\r\n@@ -232 +232 @@ MiniMove.move_selection = function(direction, opts)\r\n-  cmd('\"zx')\r\n+  cmd('\"zygv\"_x')\r\n@@ -352 +352 @@ MiniMove.move_line = function(direction, opts)\r\n-  cmd('\"zdd')\r\n+  cmd('\"zyy\"_dd')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe footgun I mentioned about restoring `\"` with a table including more than just `points_to` still applies. This causes problems when `\"` points to `z`, because `z` is overwritten with its old value before `cmd()` returns:\r\n```vim\r\nexecute \"norm ifoo\\<cr>bar\"\r\n1yank z\r\nlua require(\"mini.move\").move_line(\"up\")\r\n```\r\nExpected buffer contents:\r\n```\r\nbar\r\nfoo\r\n```\r\nActual buffer contents:\r\n```\r\nfoo\r\nfoo\r\n```",
