        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Both of these should now be fixed on latest `main`. And indeed there is now test for using only `points_to` for unnamed register (had to point it to \"z\" register). Thanks for the example!\r\n\r\n> I believe this is actually a bug in Nvim, as `:help quote1` clearly states:\r\n> \r\n> > Numbered register 1 contains the text deleted by the most recent delete or change command, **unless the command specified another register** or the text is less than one line (the small delete register is used then).\r\n\r\nThe help [was updated](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/40bc48479dca0d4a02c6445ceccab700847dcbe9/runtime/doc/change.txt#L1230) on Nightly [several months ago](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/1922f7e32b1c61e892bf4bedaf938e8b7aa44c43) following the change in Vim. The reasoning is apparently is [to be compatible with POSIX `vi`](https://github.com/vim/vim/issues/15077#issuecomment-2185013629).",
